# Web3D Review Rules

When reviewing Web3D, Three.js, or react-three-fiber code:

## Rendering Performance

Check whether code creates objects inside render loops or `useFrame`.

Avoid repeated per-frame creation of:

- Vector3
- Matrix4
- Quaternion
- Color
- Box3
- Raycaster
- Geometry
- Material
- Texture

Prefer object reuse, memoization, caching, instancing, and lazy updates.

## Resource Lifecycle

Check whether GPU resources are disposed when no longer used:

- geometry.dispose()
- material.dispose()
- texture.dispose()
- renderTarget.dispose()
- controls.dispose()

Check cleanup for:

- event listeners
- ResizeObserver
- requestAnimationFrame
- loaders
- post-processing passes

## Interaction

Check:

- camera and renderer resize synchronization
- pointer / mouse / touch cleanup
- drag and selection state consistency
- raycast performance
- fallback behavior when assets fail to load

Flag issues only when they have practical impact.